* GET.COM - REDIRECT CONSOLE INPUT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* GET.COM - REDIRECT CONSOLE INPUT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:GET FILE filespec [options]
    SYSUTLS:GET CONSOLE

Directs console input for the next program to a text file. Without SYSTEM,
input reverts to the console when that program ends. [NO ECHO] suppresses
input echo. [SYSTEM] starts reading system commands immediately from the
file until EOF or GET CONSOLE.

Example: SYSUTLS:GET FILE I0:INPUT.TXT

To restore terminal input explicitly, use SYSUTLS:GET CONSOLE. This is not
resident GET, which loads a file into memory. The supplied startup alias
uses the console-restoration form.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
